  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the following metal complexes :</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>CoCl</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>5</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>The spin-only magnetic moment value of the complex that absorbs light with shortest wavelength is B.M. (Nearest integer)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "0",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The complex that absorbs minimum wave length of light has maximum splitting</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>Crystal</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>field</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>stabilization</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>energy</mi></math></p><p>Here, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>CN</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;being <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>strong</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>field</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ligand</mi></math>&nbsp;,It&nbsp;will have cause&nbsp;CFSE So,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;will&nbsp;absorb minimum wavelength.</p><p>The hybridization of Co in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace></math></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f99a48b7-7811-4bbb-83a2-8c9fa15d1d0e-8-8-2022new.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 157px;\" />As, the complex has no unpaired electrons, spin only&nbsp; magnetic moment will be zero and it is diamagnetic in nature.</p></blockquote>",
